wash (0.9.7-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * router: disable HTTP/2 on the HTTPS fronts — h2 streams have no
    http.Hijacker, which broke the vscode /app/ ingress, the /ws fd-handoff
    behind an HTTPS wash-login, and WS upgrades ("hijacker not supported").
  * remote: serve a peer's /app/ ingress through the local origin (issue #15).
    New wash-router --listen-ingress / --peer-ingress; com.wash.remote
    forwards the socket over the same ssh; A resolves unknown tokens against
    peers and reverse-proxies. vscode/music/radio/washamp now work on remote
    hosts.
  * router: redirect plain-HTTP hits on the HTTPS listener to https://.

